# Build-context excludes for this Dockerfile. BuildKit reads
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's
# `.dockerignore`, which lets this live next to the Dockerfile it belongs to.
#
# The context is the repository root, so without this the daemon is handed a
# few hundred megabytes of installed node_modules — which the image installs
# itself, from the lockfile — and every local .env, including the backend's,
# which holds the feed signing key.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.sample
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
